// 95-safi-offline — force an offline package acquisition for the unattended
// install. live-build's archive setup (chroot_archives) always leaves a
// deb.debian.org mirror line in /etc/apt/sources.list at squash time (it
// rewrites that file AFTER the chroot hooks, so stripping it there never
// wins). Instead we cap network acquisition here: any http/https source fails
// in ~1s and is skipped, so the installer relies on the local media/cdrom and
// never hangs at "updating the list of available packages" on an air-gapped
// appliance — after which the GRUB step used to fail.
//
// This is INSTALL-time behaviour only. `safi update os` removes this file (and
// enables the parked network mirror) when an operator actually wants Debian
// network updates, so runtime OS updates are unaffected.
Acquire::Retries "0";
Acquire::http "false";
Acquire::https "false";
Acquire::cdrom "true";
Acquire::file "true";
